{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ImQDecayWidthMechanism","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.ImQDecayWidthMechanism","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.two_width_mechanisms_are_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.two_width_mechanisms_are_independent","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQDecayWidthMechanism.lean#L108-L118","doc":"**The finding.** On a real spectrum the two mechanisms disagree completely:\nA is nonzero, B is identically zero. So they are independent, and the\nframework's decay width — obtained at real `q₀` — is a reciprocal real energy\nrather than an imaginary one.\n\nScope **(a)**: this relocates candidate (iii)'s burden onto exhibiting a `Γ`\nthat mechanism A fails to produce; it does not exclude `Im q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.imaginary_mechanism_does_produce_a_width","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.imaginary_mechanism_does_produce_a_width","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQDecayWidthMechanism.lean#L100-L106","doc":"**Mechanism B is not broken — it simply is not what the framework uses.**\nIncluded so the scope of this file is legible from the Lean alone: when\n`Im E ≠ 0` mechanism B produces a perfectly good width. Nothing here excludes\n`Im q` from encoding one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.imaginary_width_zero_of_real_spectrum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.imaginary_width_zero_of_real_spectrum","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQDecayWidthMechanism.lean#L94-L98","doc":"**Mechanism B on a real spectrum gives exactly zero.** With\n`E = E₀ − iΓ/2` the width is `Γ = −2·Im E`, so a real spectrum forces `Γ = 0` —\nnot approximately, identically. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.reciprocal_width_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.reciprocal_width_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQDecayWidthMechanism.lean#L88-L92","doc":"**Mechanism A — a width from a reciprocal real energy.** `𝔇 = ℏ/Q` is\nnonzero whenever `ℏ` and `Q` are, and needs nothing complex. This is what the\nframework does: `P_skew^β = ℏ/Q_β` with `Q_β` real at real `q₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hecke_spectrum_real_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hecke_spectrum_real_iff","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQDecayWidthMechanism.lean#L79-L86","doc":"**The Hecke spectrum is real iff `Im q = 0`.** Both eigenvalue imaginary\nparts — `y` and `y/s` — vanish together, by the lemma above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hecke_second_eigenvalue_reality_locus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hecke_second_eigenvalue_reality_locus","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQDecayWidthMechanism.lean#L70-L77","doc":"**The second Hecke eigenvalue adds no reality locus.** For `q = x + iy` with\n`|q|² = s ≠ 0`, the generator's spectrum is `{q, −q⁻¹}` and\n`Im(−q⁻¹) = y/s`. That vanishes exactly where `y` does — so requiring the whole\nspectrum real is requiring `Im q = 0`, no more and no less.\n\nThis is candidate (iii)'s unitarity premise, and it is **correct**. ","signatureChunk":0}]}